From: G955N Ubuntu port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: scope native G955N opens before PCM probing

Local development-port restriction; not an upstream portability policy.
Requires 0001 disable-pro-audio backport. Hardware control identity is checked
before UCM/ACP probes and again at every production PCM open entry point.
Allow only direct RDMA0 playback and WDMA1 capture on the verified primary card.
Debug cards, other PCM endpoints and aliases are refused.
Accept only the actual ALSA UCM _ucmXXXX. namespace before a direct-hw
address, without consulting its configuration. The suffix still passes all
hardware/PCM/direction checks. Control and PCM opens use separate minimal
snd_*_open_lconf roots; caller
ALSA configuration cannot redirect the checked endpoint.

--- a/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/acp.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/acp.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
